condition_name: Blood Transfusion in the Newborn
condition_slug: blood-transfusion-in-the-newborn
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "Indicated by: - Acute haemorrhage - Anaemia"
clinical_features[0]:
investigations[0]:
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[5]: Use fresh Group O Rhesus negative blood for urgent transfusion,Transfusion recommended when PCV is < 36% and infant is critically ill,Transfusion recommended when PCV is < 30% and infant is stable or surgery is urgently needed,Single volume exchange blood transfusion with 80mL/kg of fresh cross-matched blood for severe anaemia within the first week,Intravenous frusemide 1 mg/kg to manage circulatory overload
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[2]: "Decision to transfuse should be based on the infant's haemodynamics – pulse, blood pressure",Slow drip rate to manage circulatory overload
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[7]: Transfusion reactions are extremely rare in the newborn,"Risk of transmission of infections such as HIV, Hepatitis B Virus, Hepatitis C Virus, CMV",Hyperkalaemia,Hypocalcaemia,Acidosis,Hypothermia,Circulatory overload is common
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null